+### escapeHtml.unescape(string)
+
+Decode `&quot;`, `&amp;`, `&#39;`, `&lt;`, and `&gt;`, as well as decimal
+(`&#60;`) and hexadecimal (`&#x3C;` or `&#X3c;`) numeric character references.
+Numeric references support Unicode characters, including supplementary characters.
+Unknown named entities, malformed references, and invalid Unicode code points
+(values above `0x10FFFF` or in the surrogate range `0xD800`–`0xDFFF`) are left
+unchanged. References must end with a semicolon; named entities are case-sensitive.
+
+Like `escapeHtml`, this function converts its input to a string. Each call
+decodes one layer, so `&amp;lt;` becomes `&lt;`.
+
+```js
+var unescape = require('escape-html').unescape
+
+console.log(unescape('&quot;Hello&quot; &amp; &#x3C;world&#62;'))
+// -> '"Hello" & <world>'
+```
+
